# Regexes here mark git-secrets false positives as allowed.
# Each line matched against a flagged line; if it also matches here, it's let through.
# Keep patterns narrow — only exempt the specific safe shape, not api_key checks in general.
# No literal spaces outside character classes (see CLAUDE.md's git-secrets known limitation).

# Dict/method lookups of a key literally named "api_key" (e.g. auth_config["api_key"],
# get_auth_for_generator(...)["api_key"], auth_config.get("api_key")) are references to an
# already-resolved auth dict, not a hardcoded secret value. Covers existing uses in
# src/components/llm/llm_client.py and src/components/utils.py, plus tests/eval/ragas/judge.py.
\["api_key"\]
\.get\("api_key"\)
